  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "ieee80211: Vendor Specific IE fixes",
  "description": "This MR fixes/improves two item parsing under the Vendor Specific IE:\n- The Vendor Specific data encapsulates the Vendor Specific OUI Type, as it has already its own item that does not make sense\n- The Vendor Specific data has a default dissection if there is no corresponding OUI, but WFA data does not have a default dissection if there is no corresponding subtype.\n\nThe code is not the most explicit I could do (but it is the simplest), tell me if you want me to improve it. \n\n## Before patches\n![vs_data_before](/uploads/a0eaf994de018c83a0b0f5cefa8dca07/vs_data_before.png)\n![wfa_ie_before](/uploads/8333c2f4ad862f804b83785f1e4b4bfa/wfa_ie_before.png)\n\n## After patches\n![vs_data_after](/uploads/6b0a32da07b2dbca800decb2bfc87ab4/vs_data_after.png)\n![wfa_ie_after](/uploads/5e13b9b2c7bca0cf7ad384d5261b3d5f/wfa_ie_after.png)",
